1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:05,088
This is ACME Control, a monitoring and control platform for water treatment

2
00:00:05,088 --> 00:00:09,723
plants, built with Flutter, Supabase, and a TypeScript API on Vercel.

3
00:00:09,723 --> 00:00:11,742
Each demo account has a role.

4
00:00:11,742 --> 00:00:13,713
Let's sign in as the operator.

5
00:00:14,426 --> 00:00:18,982
The process view shows the live plant: two tanks, pumps, valves, levels,

6
00:00:18,982 --> 00:00:23,791
pressures and flows, with water moving through the pipes in a 3D diagram you

7
00:00:23,791 --> 00:00:24,424
can orbit.

8
00:00:24,424 --> 00:00:28,438
Every asset shows its requested state next to its actual state.

9
00:00:29,138 --> 00:00:31,575
Commands only work in manual mode.

10
00:00:31,575 --> 00:00:36,941
I switch pump P-101 to manual so it keeps running, then switch the inlet valve

11
00:00:36,941 --> 00:00:38,523
to manual and close it.

12
00:00:38,523 --> 00:00:41,804
The valve travels, and the inflow drops to zero.

13
00:00:42,506 --> 00:00:46,734
On the simulation page, I can choose scenarios and advance time.

14
00:00:46,734 --> 00:00:48,609
Let's jump four hours ahead.

15
00:00:49,322 --> 00:00:52,793
Back on the process view, the raw water tank is empty.

16
00:00:52,793 --> 00:00:57,136
The pump is still requested to run, but the interlock keeps it stopped, and

17
00:00:57,136 --> 00:00:58,178
alarms are raised.

18
00:00:58,874 --> 00:01:02,417
Alarms are prioritised, and operators acknowledge them.

19
00:01:02,417 --> 00:01:06,227
Trends show the history of levels, flows and pressures.

20
00:01:06,938 --> 00:01:11,419
Engineers propose setpoint changes, and a supervisor reviews them.

21
00:01:11,419 --> 00:01:15,997
Here, the supervisor approves a pending proposal, and the new value takes

22
00:01:15,997 --> 00:01:17,188
effect immediately.

23
00:01:17,882 --> 00:01:20,981
Maintenance work orders support lockout and tagout.

24
00:01:20,981 --> 00:01:26,822
At Harbor Point, pump P-102 is locked out for a seal replacement, so it cannot

25
00:01:26,822 --> 00:01:27,122
run.

26
00:01:27,122 --> 00:01:30,079
There are also shift handovers and a plants overview.

27
00:01:30,794 --> 00:01:36,777
On phones, the diagram becomes vertical, with tabs for plant, alarms, assets

28
00:01:36,777 --> 00:01:37,486
and more.

29
00:01:37,486 --> 00:01:42,388
If the connection drops, the app keeps showing the last data, read-only, and

30
00:01:42,388 --> 00:01:44,001
disables control actions.

31
00:01:44,714 --> 00:01:48,594
Everything is stored in Supabase and shared between web and mobile.

32
00:01:48,594 --> 00:01:50,637
That's ACME Control.
